WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.094 --> 00:00:01.901
- I grew up in the parallel universe

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.010
that used the E.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.189
I remember it was the Berenstein Bears.

00:00:05.189 --> 00:00:08.856
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:18.489 --> 00:00:20.292
- So if there's really good memory

00:00:20.292 --> 00:00:21.995
and there's really bad memory,

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:23.499
I would say I'm in the middle.

00:00:23.499 --> 00:00:25.285
- Long term memory, great.

00:00:25.285 --> 00:00:28.420
Short term memory, (murmuring).

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.644
- My memory's okay,

00:00:30.644 --> 00:00:32.624
but like going downhill as I get older.

00:00:32.624 --> 00:00:36.473
- So I feel like I have
a pretty good memory.

00:00:36.473 --> 00:00:37.807
- Oh, is it Sex in the City

00:00:37.807 --> 00:00:38.968
or Sex and the City?

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:40.165
That's the question.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:43.336
- I have gone on Sex and
the City benders before.

00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:44.942
- Sex and the City, baby.

00:00:44.942 --> 00:00:46.407
(bell chiming)

00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:47.240
- No, is it not?

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.073
Am I wrong?

00:00:48.073 --> 00:00:48.906
- [Man] Incorrect.

00:00:48.906 --> 00:00:50.296
- Incorrect?

00:00:50.296 --> 00:00:51.369
- You have sex in a city.

00:00:51.369 --> 00:00:54.499
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:55.806
- It's, "Mirror, mirror on the wall.

00:00:55.806 --> 00:00:57.727
"Who's the fairest of them all?"

00:00:57.727 --> 00:00:59.409
- Well, isn't it mirror, mirror?

00:00:59.409 --> 00:01:02.037
(bell chiming)

00:01:02.037 --> 00:01:02.981
- What?

00:01:02.981 --> 00:01:05.235
- Magic mirror, no.

00:01:05.235 --> 00:01:06.068
- No it's not.

00:01:06.068 --> 00:01:07.151
You're lying.

00:01:08.743 --> 00:01:11.855
♫ It's a beautiful day in the neighborhood

00:01:11.855 --> 00:01:13.459
- The neighborhood?

00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:15.235
This neighborhood?

00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:16.193
Which neighborhood?

00:01:16.193 --> 00:01:17.769
(bell chiming)

00:01:17.769 --> 00:01:19.132
- A beautiful day in this,

00:01:19.132 --> 00:01:20.760
he does not sing it like that.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.231
- Dude, this is also bad
songwriting if it's this.

00:01:23.231 --> 00:01:24.064
- Is it?

00:01:24.064 --> 00:01:24.897
I don't know.

00:01:24.897 --> 00:01:25.730
That doesn't sound right.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.202
Someone should have given him a note.

00:01:27.202 --> 00:01:28.250
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.849
- Blank, "I am your father."

00:01:30.849 --> 00:01:31.682
- Dad?

00:01:31.682 --> 00:01:34.143
- Now I know it's not gonna
be whatever's obvious.

00:01:34.143 --> 00:01:35.242
- Is it Luke?

00:01:35.242 --> 00:01:36.641
- Guessing it's this.

00:01:36.641 --> 00:01:38.304
(bell chiming)

00:01:38.304 --> 00:01:39.137
- This is dumb.

00:01:39.137 --> 00:01:40.560
That is so silly.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.548
- I'm gonna go home and cry now.

00:01:42.548 --> 00:01:44.681
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:01:44.681 --> 00:01:45.514
- Shazam?

00:01:45.514 --> 00:01:46.474
Shablam?

00:01:46.474 --> 00:01:51.355
- I don't know of any movie
featuring Sinbad as a genie.

00:01:51.355 --> 00:01:52.696
- Shazam.

00:01:52.696 --> 00:01:54.247
- There was no movie.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.786
(bell chiming)

00:01:56.786 --> 00:01:57.663
- What?

00:01:57.663 --> 00:01:59.575
There's no movie called Shazam?

00:01:59.575 --> 00:02:00.607
- Who am I?

00:02:00.607 --> 00:02:03.134
- I'm just gonna look at that real quick.

00:02:03.134 --> 00:02:04.249
That's not possible.

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:05.524
I've seen the movie Shazam.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.107
He's a genie in it.

00:02:08.185 --> 00:02:10.530
- The Berenstein Bears.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.441
- Alright, well, now I'm upset.

00:02:12.441 --> 00:02:14.306
(bell chiming)

00:02:14.306 --> 00:02:15.522
- No it's not.

00:02:15.522 --> 00:02:16.667
- Berenstain,

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.751
that says Berenstain.

00:02:18.751 --> 00:02:20.979
- I don't know who's lobbying for big A,

00:02:20.979 --> 00:02:22.570
but I'm just gonna say it's some nonsense,

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.177
and those bears deserve better.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.712
- I hate life.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.352
(upbeat instrumental music)

00:02:27.352 --> 00:02:29.528
- (sighing) Everything has been a lie.

00:02:29.528 --> 00:02:31.071
- I refuse to change my mind.

00:02:31.071 --> 00:02:33.575
I think those signs are
from a alternate universe.

00:02:33.575 --> 00:02:35.044
- I don't think it's implausible to assume

00:02:35.044 --> 00:02:38.014
that there's billions
of alternate timelines

00:02:38.014 --> 00:02:40.894
all occurring at once on
different planes of existence.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:44.001
I mean, you know, there's no
movie called Shazam apparently,

00:02:44.001 --> 00:02:46.015
so I guess anything's (beeping) possible.

00:02:46.015 --> 00:02:48.074
- I'd like to think that I'm
from the parallel universe

00:02:48.074 --> 00:02:49.928
with a lot of dogs,

00:02:49.928 --> 00:02:52.318
lots of color blue, weird people.

00:02:52.318 --> 00:02:53.288
I'd be fine with that.

00:02:53.288 --> 00:02:54.508
- Shazam is real.

00:02:54.508 --> 00:02:55.632
Shazam is real.

